{"absent":["Locking, concurrency and ordering rules for capability state, sanitized registers and overrides are not shown.","How and when sanitized ID registers, capability bits and override descriptors are initialized is not shown.","Numeric encodings of ID register fields, capability identifiers and override structure layouts are not shown.","Interrupt controller mask accessors, IRQ priority masking detection and DAIF bit definitions are not shown.","Composite MIDR values beyond the truncated point and any behavior outside the routed ranges are not shown.","Error handling or power management beyond IRQ context save and restore is not shown."],"dossier":"D11","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_4kb_granule","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_64kb_granule","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_16kb_granule","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_mixed_endian_el0","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_mixed_endian"],"text":"System granule and endian queries report platform support derived from the sanitized memory model register. The three granule checks accept only values inside a supported interval. One mixed endian check uses a dedicated EL0 helper while the general check requires a single encoding value."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_fpsimd","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_sve","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_sme","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_sme2","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_fa64","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_fpmr","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_cnp","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_mte","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_tlb_range","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_poe","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_gcs","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_mpam","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_mpam_hcr","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_bbml3"],"text":"System extension queries report availability of FPSIMD, SVE, SME, second generation SME, FA64, FPMR, CNP, MTE, TLB range, POE, GCS, MPAM, MPAM HCR and BBML3 through an alternative capability mechanism, with differing likely present or likely absent patching hints."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_32bit_el0"],"text":"32-bit EL0 support is true when either a mismatched 32-bit static branch is active or the sanitized processor feature register indicates 32-bit EL0 capability."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_tpidr2","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_sme","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_address_auth","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_generic_auth","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_has_full_ptr_auth","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_uses_hw_pan","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_uses_ttbr0_pan","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_has_prio_mask_debugging","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_bti_kernel","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::system_supports_bti"],"text":"Several system predicates are compositions. TPIDR2 availability equals SME availability. Full pointer authentication needs both address and generic authentication. Software TTBR0 PAN is active only with its configuration enabled and hardware PAN absent. Priority mask debugging needs its configuration and IRQ priority masking. Kernel BTI needs its configuration and the boot BTI capability."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::id_aa64mmfr0_parange_to_phys_shift"],"text":"Physical address size mapping converts known PARange encodings for 32, 36, 40, 42, 44, 48 and 52 bits to the same numeric shift. Any other encoding, including future larger values, yields the configured maximum physical bits limit as a safe clamp."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::get_vmid_bits"],"text":"VMID width is sixteen only when the relevant memory model field holds the sixteen bit encoding, otherwise eight is returned, including for any reserved encoding."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_hw_af","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_pan","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_bti","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_pac","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_lva","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_lpa2","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_amu_feat"],"text":"Per CPU queries expose hardware access flag support, PAN presence, BTI, pointer authentication, large virtual addressing and LPA2. The AMU feature query for a given CPU constantly reports unavailable in these fragments."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::arm64_apply_feature_override","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::arm64_test_sw_feature_override","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::kaslr_disabled_cmdline"],"text":"Feature override handling first narrows the stored override value to the target field width, then applies it only when every set value bit is also set in the mask, and finally extracts the field as an unsigned value. Software feature testing applies the same logic to a zero base with narrow width, and the KASLR disabled command line test is one software override bit."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_bti","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_pac","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_lva","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_has_lpa2"],"text":"CPU BTI and pointer authentication checks are disabled without their respective build options. Pointer authentication is present when any of three adjusted architecture fields is nonzero. Large virtual address and LPA2 checks merge an override mask and value into the live register before extraction, with LPA2 additionally requiring its build option and a signed threshold comparison."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpuidle.h::arm_cpuidle_irq_context.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpuidle.h::arm_cpuidle_irq_context.alt_2"],"text":"The idle IRQ context has two build variants. One holds two machine word members recording the interrupt controller priority mask and the saved interrupt mask bits. The other is an empty type with no members."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cpuidle.h::arm_cpuidle_irq_context.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpuidle.h::arm_cpuidle_save_irq_context.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpuidle.h::arm_cpuidle_restore_irq_context.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpuidle.h::arm_cpuidle_save_irq_context.alt_2","arch/arm64/include/asm/cpuidle.h::arm_cpuidle_restore_irq_context.alt_2"],"text":"Idle IRQ save and restore form a paired protocol. When IRQ priority masking is in use, save preserves interrupt mask state, blocks IRQ and FIQ, preserves the controller mask, then raises it to an IRQ on level. Restore writes back the saved controller mask and interrupt mask. Without priority masking both operations do nothing."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::INVALID_HWID","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MPIDR_UP_BITMASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MPIDR_MT_BITMASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MPIDR_HWID_BITMASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MPIDR_LEVEL_BITS_SHIFT","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MPIDR_LEVEL_BITS","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MPIDR_LEVEL_MASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MPIDR_LEVEL_SHIFT"],"text":"Affinity and topology decoding uses a sentinel for invalid hardware identifiers, bit masks for UP and MT fields, a mask selecting hardware identifier bits, and level parameters defining three bit wide levels with a derived mask and per level shift."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_REVISION_MASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_REVISION","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_PARTNUM_SHIFT","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_PARTNUM_MASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_PARTNUM","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_ARCHITECTURE_SHIFT","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_ARCHITECTURE_MASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_ARCHITECTURE","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_VARIANT_SHIFT","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_VARIANT_MASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_VARIANT","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_IMPLEMENTOR_SHIFT","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_IMPLEMENTOR_MASK","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_IMPLEMENTOR","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_CPU_MODEL","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_CPU_VAR_REV","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::MIDR_CPU_MODEL_MASK"],"text":"Main ID register layout defines revision, part number, architecture, variant and implementor field positions and masks with helpers to extract each, plus constructors for a CPU model from implementor and part and for variant revision, and a mask covering model identity fields."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_ARM","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_APM","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_CAVIUM","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_BRCM","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_QCOM","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_NVIDIA","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_FUJITSU","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_HISI","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_APPLE","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_AMPERE","arch/arm64/include/asm/cputype.h::ARM_CPU_IMP_MICROSOFT"],"text